# Resolution
Fixed in commit [`4ec9a4df`](https://github.com/justincormack/argmin/commit/4ec9a4df) (`Reject future epoch heartbeats`), which made the control plane reject heartbeats whose `observed_epoch` is greater than the current control-plane epoch before mutating node liveness, lease state, PG observations, or PG peering state. The fix preserves the intended stale-epoch heartbeat behavior for restarted or lagging storage nodes while making future-epoch reports fail closed.

Follow-up commit [`746bbb8c`](https://github.com/justincormack/argmin/commit/746bbb8c7ff26ff2a86c37d0122cfe8f1e6700be) (`Harden metadata checkpoint startup races`) adjusted control-plane-managed storage-node startup so bootstrap heartbeats no longer reuse the static `ARGMIN_STORAGE_CLUSTER_EPOCH` value from the legacy no-control-plane path. Startup now reports `ClusterEpoch::INITIAL` and learns the authoritative epoch from the returned runtime map, avoiding accidental future-epoch bootstrap heartbeats under the stricter guard.

# Summary
Introduced bug: mismatched-epoch heartbeats now persist attacker-controlled/stale/future liveness fields and clear PG observations instead of being side-effect-free. This enables a local/control-plane-adjacent actor able to submit a storage-node heartbeat to force affected PGs out of service or trigger repeering.
In SingleAuthorityControlPlane::heartbeat, the new mismatched-epoch branch handles all `heartbeat.observed_epoch != current_epoch` cases the same way. It updates `last_observed_epoch` to the heartbeat-provided epoch, refreshes the lease deadline, clears PG observations, and may mark all PGs involving the node as peering when incarnation or endpoint changes. There is no check that the observed epoch is less than or equal to the control-plane epoch, so a future observed epoch is accepted. Since `NodeControlRecord::can_serve_primary` requires `last_observed_epoch == current_epoch`, and active PG serving also depends on current PG observations, one malformed heartbeat can make an otherwise healthy active primary stop being considered serving. Before this commit, mismatched-epoch heartbeats returned a non-serving lease without mutating the control-plane snapshot.

