## Report
Validated the finding against commit 09407f81a026d462789589951f866e6aaaee47fb. Code evidence: crates/storage/src/control_plane.rs:213-219 requires last_observed_epoch == current cluster_epoch for serving eligibility. The mismatched-epoch heartbeat branch at control_plane.rs:2344 handles any observed_epoch != current_epoch without rejecting future epochs; at 2368-2374 it stores heartbeat.observed_epoch, refreshes heartbeat/lease fields, and clears pg_observations; at 2376-2380 it marks PGs peering when endpoint/incarnation changes; at 2388 it returns serving=false. The helper at 5715-5727 only checks cluster-map-history floor, and with an empty/default summary returns Ok without comparing heartbeat.observed_epoch to the current epoch. I added a targeted integration PoC at crates/storage/tests/future_epoch_heartbeat_poc.rs. The PoC first creates an active node/PG with a stored active PG observation and deterministic primary Some(node 1), then submits a forged heartbeat with future_epoch = before_epoch + 100 plus attacker-controlled endpoint/incarnation. The heartbeat is accepted via unwrap at PoC line 112. Assertions at lines 114-127 confirm the side effects: non-serving lease, epoch bump, persisted endpoint, persisted future last_observed_epoch, refreshed lease deadline, cleared PG observation, active PG moved to Peering, and deterministic primary becomes None. Command output: `cargo test -p storage --test future_epoch_heartbeat_poc -- --nocapture` completed with `test future_epoch_heartbeat_persists_liveness_clears_observations_and_repeers ... ok`. Crash attempt: the PoC does not crash because this is a logic/availability bug, but it dynamically reproduces the vulnerable state transition. Valgrind attempt was made but unavailable in the container: `bash: command not found: valgrind`. Debugger validation: LLDB breakpoint at control_plane.rs:2368 stopped in SingleAuthorityControlPlane::heartbeat for the forged heartbeat with `heartbeat.observed_epoch = 105`, `current_epoch = 5`, `lease_deadline_ms = 4000`, and the stack showed the call from future_epoch_heartbeat_poc.rs:112; continuing completed the test successfully.

